cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
title: "OpenSWMM Engine"
message: "If you use OpenSWMM Engine, developed by HydroCouple, please cite the version you used as below."
abstract: >-
  OpenSWMM Engine, developed by HydroCouple, is an open-source hydrology,
  hydraulics and water-quality simulation engine for stormwater, wastewater
  and combined sewer systems. It is built on the EPA Storm Water Management
  Model (SWMM) 5.x and provides a reentrant C++20 engine, a public C API,
  Python bindings, two-dimensional surface flow and a command-line solver.
authors:
  - family-names: Buahin
    given-names: Caleb
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9859-2264"
  - name: HydroCouple Developers
version: "6.0.0-alpha.4"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/HydroCouple/openswmm.engine"
url: "https://hydrocouple.org/openswmm.engine"
keywords:
  - stormwater
  - urban drainage
  - hydrology
  - hydraulics
  - water quality
  - SWMM
  - two-dimensional surface flow
references:
